<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">A Door to Our Hearts</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;We saved the universe, so why does it feel like sometimes I never saved anything? Space was supposed to be peaceful, we were supposed to be together, so why do I feel like we're only growing apart? We went through so much before, fought so hard to be here with each other. I just want things to be okay. I want things to stay fixed. So why does it seem like everything breaks?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adora has woken up in Castle Grayskull, but nothing makes sense. She doesn't know how she got there, or even when. Something has gone horribly wrong and she can't even trust &lt;em&gt;when&lt;/em&gt; things are happening. Catra is concealing something from her and the BFS has been injured in some mysterious event that Adora can't recall. Does the answer lie in her past, present, or future?&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>4theHonourofGrÃ¤yskÃ¼ll (AVAwolfpack), But_Its_For_Science (DakianDelomast), DakianDelomast</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
